Meilisearch on FenrirOS
=======================

Nothing is enabled or configured for you: the service is shipped, not turned on.

  /etc/dinit.d/meilisearch          the service (dinitctl enable meilisearch)
  /etc/meilisearch/config.toml      its configuration (loopback only, development mode)
  /var/lib/meilisearch              the data (the _meilisearch user owns it)

Before using it beyond this machine: set env = "production" and a master_key in
config.toml (production mode refuses to start without one). Analytics are off
(no_analytics = true).

The built-in search dashboard (the mini-dashboard, as upstream's default build)
is at http://127.0.0.1:7700/ in development mode.

The source tree has an Enterprise Edition part (LICENSE-EE, the sharding and
replication features of Meilisearch's commercial edition); this package builds
it as upstream's default build does. Read LICENSE-EE before using those features
in production.
